  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> be the centre of the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Let the tangents at two points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> on the circle intersect at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>area</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>APQ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>area</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>BPQ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to&nbsp;<u>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</u> .",
    "image": null
  },
